s of the tangent line to $C$ at $P.$" 13194139535580 17592186045443 true] [17592186518836 1072 #uuid "03efd4b4-041a-5564-818d-06a45aad1a76" 13194139535580 17592186045443 true] [17592186518836 1074 "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $y=-4.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(2,-4,-1)$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(2,-4)}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}$ at $(2,-4):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(2,-4) & =-4(2) \\\\ & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(2,-4)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(2,-4)}(x-(2)) \\\\ z-(-1) & =(-8)(x-(2)) \\\\ z & =15 - 8 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(2,-4,-1)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y=-4 \\\\ z=15 - 8 x\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535580 17592186045443 true] [17592186518837 1080 "\\{\\begin{aligned}y=- \\pi \\\\ z=- \\left(1 + \\pi\\right) \\left(x + 2\\right)\\end{aligned}" 13194139535580 17592186045443 true] [17592186518837 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535580 17592186045443 true] [17592186518837 1083 #uuid "06cf7030-0c6b-58ec-b96b-cc1eaee16f6b" 13194139535580 17592186045443 true] [17592186518838 1075 #edb/ref 17592186518851 13194139535580 17592186045443 true] [17592186518838 1075 #edb/ref 17592186518865 13194139535580 17592186045443 true] [17592186518838 1075 #edb/ref 17592186518879 13194139535580 17592186045443 true] [17592186518838 1075 #edb/ref 17592186518883 13194139535580 17592186045443 true] [17592186518838 1075 #edb/ref 17592186518900 13194139535580 17592186045443 true] [17592186518838 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139535580 17592186045443 true] [17592186518838 1077 "selection" 13194139535580 17592186045443 true] [17592186518838 1078 #edb/ref 17592186518883 13194139535580 17592186045443 true] [17592186518838 1079 #u